Materials Project ID: mp-1265 (rocksalt MgO, space group Fm-3m #225, confirmed by spglib at symprec=0.01). Atom count before primitive reduction: 2; after reduction: 2 (the MP CIF was already the 2-atom rhombohedral primitive cell; the conventional FCC cell would be 8). Space group unchanged by reduction.

Workflow outline:
1. structures/check_primitive.py: verified SG 225 and wrote mgo_primitive.cif.
2. generate_structures.py: read mgo_primitive.cif with ase.io.read; wrote 51 CIFs (structure_000 = unperturbed base; 001-050 perturbed) via ase.io.write. Perturbation: Gaussian atomic displacements sigma=0.08 Ang (Atoms.rattle) -- a chemically reasonable room-temperature thermal RMS displacement, small vs the ~2.1 Ang Mg-O bond -- plus a symmetric random lattice strain drawn uniformly in +/-1% per component (Atoms.set_cell scale_atoms=True). Asserted nat=2/ntyp=2 per structure (INVARIANT 1).
3. get_pseudopotential fetched Mg.upf and O.upf into template/ (nc, sr, pbesol, stringent, upf). Reported cutoff hint 42.0 Ha for both; converted to Ry per INVARIANT 5: ecutwfc = 2*42 = 84 Ry, ecutrho = 4*84 = 336 Ry (NC standard).
4. setup_jobs.py: for each structure built calculations/NNN/ with pseudos copied in (pseudo_dir='.'), pw.in (SCF) and bands.in (NSCF along explicit seekpath-derived k-path) both via ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in with a FLAT input_data dict (INVARIANT 6, validated), bands_post.in (&BANDS filband='NNN.bands.dat'), and band_labels.dat. K-path derived per structure via seekpath (symprec=0.01), re-projected through Cartesian onto atoms.cell.reciprocal() with the 2*pi factor added (INVARIANT 3); SG self-consistency asserted. SCF k-mesh: Monkhorst-Pack 8x8x8 (dense for the 2-atom insulator cell). occupations='fixed' (wide-gap insulator), conv_thr=1e-8, nbnd=16 padded. validate_qe_input passed for calculations/000 pw.in and bands.in.
5. run_espresso_workflow on calculations/000 ONLY returned success:true (scf, bands_scf, bands_post all completed). pw.out ground truth: number of electrons = 16.00, Kohn-Sham states = 8. Actual Zval Mg=10 (semicore), O=6 -- the naive get_pseudopotential hints (Mg 3, O 2) were WRONG, confirming INVARIANT 2; occupied bands = 16/2 = 8, so nbnd=16 is sufficient (no fix needed).
6. plot_bands.py: parsed the real, non-empty 000.bands.dat (QE plotband/filband, nbnd=16 nks=180), read number of electrons from pw.out in code (n_occ=8, not hardcoded), built cumulative k-path distance in 2*pi/alat from the k-coords so ticks and band data share units (INVARIANT 4 -- asserted tick range vs band-x range), broke the line only at genuine '|' discontinuities, restricted y to +/-10 eV around VBM, and saved calculations/000/bands_000.pdf.

ASE functions used: ase.io.read / ase.io.write (structure I/O, CIF), Atoms.rattle / Atoms.set_cell (perturbations), ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in (pw.x input files). Symmetry/k-path via spglib + seekpath. Output parsed directly (QE plotband + pw.out) in code.

Band gap obtained: 4.78 eV (VBM 8.099 eV, CBM 12.880 eV, aligned to VBM). This is a direct gap at Gamma. Note: this is the DFT-PBEsol Kohn-Sham gap, which for MgO is known to underestimate the ~7.8 eV experimental gap -- expected DFT behavior, not an error.

Assumptions / expert-review items: (a) spin-unpolarized, non-magnetic MgO (occupations='fixed') -- correct for closed-shell rocksalt MgO. (b) Perturbation magnitudes (0.08 Ang displacement, 1% strain) are physically motivated defaults; if a specific ensemble/temperature is targeted an expert may want to tune sigma or draw strain anisotropically. (c) DFT gap underestimation is inherent to PBEsol -- a hybrid/GW calculation would be needed for a quantitative gap. (d) Only structure_000 was run through DFT as instructed; the other 50 inputs are generated but not executed. All three scripts ran end-to-end with empty stderr and none import pymatgen; INVARIANTS verified against the actual calculations/000/pw.in and 000.bands.dat.
